cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its processed data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Praxistérkép — An Open Map and Analysis of Hungarian Primary Care Vacancies"
abstract: >-
  An open, reproducible map and analysis of Hungary's primary care districts
  (general practice and dentistry), rebuilt every month from public data of
  the National Health Insurance Fund (NEAK) and other state publishers. It
  shows which districts have no contracted physician, for how long, how many
  residents they serve, how far the nearest care is by road and by bus, and
  what goes with vacancy across the country's 197 districts (járás): avoidable
  mortality, income, education, unemployment and out-migration, with partial
  correlations that hold income and education constant. It follows each
  state settlement grant through the monthly archive to what became of the
  district, forecasts vacancies a year ahead with a back-test, sets Hungary
  beside the 27 member states and the United Kingdom (Eurostat, OECD) and
  its border regions beside their neighbours, and publishes
  a static, bilingual page for each of the 3,177 settlements. Every figure
  traces to an archived source file; the pipeline fails rather than publish
  a partial or estimated number. Informational, not an official publication.
version: 1.52.0
date-released: 2026-10-19
url: "https://praxisterkep.hu"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZoliQua/Praxisterkep"
license: MIT
